{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"actor","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"HostKeyring","kind":"identifier"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"content":[{"level":2,"text":"Overview","type":"heading","anchor":"overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A keychain read can wait as long as a person takes to answer a SecurityAgent prompt, which the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"login keychain shows for items an earlier, differently signed build wrote. So the helper’s own"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"keychain is read first, and the host serves with its key and paired devices as soon as they"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"are there; the login keychain is read after, once, only for the items the helper’s own lacks."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Its answer joins the trust list then. A key is made only after it has answered, so a key that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"may be there is never replaced; only then does a host with no key of its own wait for it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once read, a mark in the helper’s own keychain says so, and no later launch reads it again."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost"]]},"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"patch":0,"major":0},"metadata":{"externalID":"s:15HeadwireMacHost0C7KeyringC","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"HostKeyring"}],"modules":[{"name":"HeadwireMacHost"}],"title":"HostKeyring","roleHeading":"Class","role":"symbol","symbolKind":"class","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"actor"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"HostKeyring"}]},"topicSections":[{"title":"Structures","generated":true,"identifiers":["doc:\/\/HeadwireMacHost\/documentation\/HeadwireMacHost\/HostKeyring\